hoacana Meat Market","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Latin American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["La Michoacana Meat Market is a chain of Hispanic specialty stores and grocery stores in the United States, headquartered in Spring Branch, Houston, Texas. Rafael Ortega, founder, has about 135 stores throughout Texas and Oklahoma. The chain is named after the Mexican state of Michoacán located on Mexico's Pacific coast."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-la-michoacana-meat-market"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Michoacana_Meat_Market"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Latin American cuisine","cuisine/latin-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Latin American cuisine","links":[["Bollo","dish/bollo"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Cardenas (supermarket)","dish/cardenas-supermarket"],["El Cielo (restaurant)","dish/el-cielo-restaurant"],["Frijoles negros","dish/frijoles-negros"],["Mi Pueblo Food Center","dish/mi-pueblo-food-center"],["Quince cheese","dish/quince-cheese"],["Rice and beans","dish/rice-and-beans"],["Tamale","dish/tamale"],["Vallarta Supermarkets","dish/vallarta-supermarkets"]]}]},"dish/maeun-tang":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/maeun-tang","n":"Maeun-tang","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Maeun-tang or spicy fish stew is a dish in Korean cuisine. It is a hot spicy fish soup boiled with gochujang (Korean red chili pepper paste), '고춧가루'(chili powder), and various vegetables. The name is a combination of two words: '매운', which derives from '맵다', meaning \"hot and spicy\"; and '탕(湯)', meaning \"soup\". As its main ingredient, fresh or saltwater fish is cut into several pieces and boiled with green vegetables such as watercress and garland chrysanthemum. Onion, radish, chilis, crown daisy, garlic, and sometimes zucchini and bean curd are added to the mixture to absorb the chili pepper paste which is the main flavoring of this dish. It is then seasoned with chili powder, garlic, soy sauce, and additional gochujang may be added once more to taste."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-maeun-tang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maeun-tang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Alaska pollock","ingredient/alaska-pollock"],["Chili powder","ingredient/chili-powder"],["Gochujang","ingredient/gochujang"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Maangchi","ref":"site/maangchi-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"maangchi.com","note":"Maangchi's Korean recipe site and YouTube channel, one of the best known English sources for Korean cooking.","url":"https://www.maangchi.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Korean Bapsang","ref":"site/koreanbapsang-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Korean cuisine","links":[["Bap (rice dish)","dish/bap-rice-dish"],["Bibim-guksu","dish/bibim-guksu"],["Bibimbap","dish/bibimbap"],["Bosintang","dish/bosintang"],["Cheonggukjang","dish/cheonggukjang"],["Danji","dish/danji"],["Doenjang","dish/doenjang"],["Garak-guksu","dish/garak-guksu"],["Gochujang","dish/gochujang"],["Gopchang","dish/gopchang"],["Han Oak","dish/han-oak"],["Hwajeon","dish/hwajeon"],["Jijimi","dish/jijimi"],["Jokbal","dish/jokbal"],["Kim Jong Grillin'","dish/kim-jong-grillin"],["Korean restaurant","dish/korean-restaurant"],["Maekjeok","dish/maekjeok"],["Makchang","dish/makchang"],["Mandu-guk","dish/mandu-guk"],["Mandu-gwa","dish/mandu-gwa"],["Maum (restaurant)","dish/maum-restaurant"],["Meat jun","dish/meat-jun"],["Meju","dish/meju"],["Morkovcha","dish/morkovcha"],["Parachute (restaurant)","dish/parachute-restaurant"],["Revelry (restaurant)","dish/revelry-restaurant